WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:06.710
He is the epitome of pure, unadulterated evil;
the mastermind guru with the swastika on his

00:00:06.710 --> 00:00:09.530
forehead and the wild, crazed look in his
eyes.

00:00:09.530 --> 00:00:14.129
He was responsible for the one of the most
heinous crimes of our time, controlling his

00:00:14.129 --> 00:00:16.410
minions like a puppeteer.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:23.910
In this week’s Biographics we discover the
dark, disturbing story of Charles Manson.

00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:32.070
A Dysfunctional Beginning

00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:37.430
Charles Milles Manson was born on November
12th, 1934 to sixteen-year old Kathleen Maddox

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:42.310
and a 24-year old transient laborer known
as ‘Colonel Scott’.

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:47.239
Kathleen was a promiscuous teenager who drank
too much and earned money to fuel her habits

00:00:47.239 --> 00:00:48.790
be selling her body.

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:52.900
The baby was known as ‘No Name Maddox’
for the first few weeks of life until his

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.550
mother settled on Charlie.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:58.590
He never knew his father; he cleared out as
soon he heard that Kathleen was pregnant.

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:04.040
Kathleen was too young, immature and unpredictable
to provide a stable environment for a young

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:05.040
child.

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.319
She appeared to have no maternal instinct
and would leave the child to fend for himself

00:01:08.319 --> 00:01:10.579
while she went off on one of her benders.

00:01:10.579 --> 00:01:15.159
As an adult, Charlie often related that his
mother was once in a café with him on her

00:01:15.159 --> 00:01:18.380
knee when the waitress offered to buy the
baby from her.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:23.090
Kathleen’s asking price was a pitcher of
beer and, having consumed it, she simply walked

00:01:23.090 --> 00:01:25.210
out and left Charlie to the woman.

00:01:25.210 --> 00:01:29.850
According to Charlie, his uncle took four
days to track him down and return him home.

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:33.609
When Charlie was six years old, his mother
and uncle decided to rob a gas station.

00:01:33.609 --> 00:01:38.119
They were both caught, convicted and sent
for five years to Moundsville State Prison.

00:01:38.119 --> 00:01:41.950
The boy was put into the care of his strictly
religious grandparents but after a few months

00:01:41.950 --> 00:01:44.200
he went to live with his aunt and uncle in
McMecham, West Virginia.

00:01:44.200 --> 00:01:48.340
This environment was very different to anything
Charlie had known previously.

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:51.329
His aunt, unlike her sister, was regimented
and disciplined.

00:01:51.329 --> 00:01:53.039
She was also strictly religious.

00:01:53.039 --> 00:01:57.430
Her husband, Bill, was even more fervent in
his faith than his wife.

00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:01.139
A strict disciplinarian, he considered Charlie
to be a sissy.

00:02:01.139 --> 00:02:04.619
On his first day of school he sent the boy
to class in a dress in order to teach him

00:02:04.619 --> 00:02:06.130
how to fight.

00:02:06.130 --> 00:02:09.780
Charlie soon adapted to this very different
kind of life and actually grew to enjoy his

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:11.330
new regimented routine.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:14.810
The two years between six and eight were to
prove to be the most stable of his young life.

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:18.400
But then his mother was released from prison
and immediately took him back.

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.190
Kathleen was more unstable than ever.

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:25.630
She preferred a life of promiscuity and alcohol
abuse to maternal domesticity.

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:29.201
Constantly in trouble with the law and with
no money for food and board, the constantly

00:02:29.201 --> 00:02:30.810
moved around the midWest.

00:02:30.810 --> 00:02:33.280
At the age of nine, Charlie dropped out of
school.

00:02:33.280 --> 00:02:37.990
The transient life that he was forced to live
shaped the type of boy that Charlie became.

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:41.530
He kept to himself, living his life through
his imagination.

00:02:41.530 --> 00:02:46.140
He was constantly watching, taking things
in and dreaming of a future free of his no

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:47.140
hoper mother.

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:49.960
He also learnt how to become a very accomplished
thief.

00:02:49.960 --> 00:02:53.640
At age nine, Charlie was caught stealing and
sent to reform school.

00:02:53.640 --> 00:02:55.530
Three years later, he was caught again.

00:02:55.530 --> 00:02:59.410
This time he was packed off to the Gibault
School for Boys in Terre Haute, Indiana.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:02.460
Before he was taken away, Kathleen promised
to visit him often.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:04.190
Of course, she never did.

00:03:04.190 --> 00:03:07.090
Just ten months in to his incarceration, Charlie
escaped.

00:03:07.090 --> 00:03:11.040
He robbed a grocery store to get some money
and, when that ran out, stole other things,

00:03:11.040 --> 00:03:12.110
including a bicycle.

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:16.900
He got caught in the act of making off with
the bike and soon found himself back in confinement.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:19.490
This time he was sent to an Indiana juvenile
center.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:24.550
But after just two days, he stole some wire
cutters and freed, not only himself, but 30

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:25.550
other boys.

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:28.460
This time the escaped young felon stole, not
a bike, but a car.

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:32.319
But the 13-year old could hardly see over
the steering wheel and was apprehended within

00:03:32.319 --> 00:03:33.690
hours of his escape.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:36.390
When he ended up in juvenile court, he was
surprised to see his mother.

00:03:36.390 --> 00:03:40.380
His spirits were dashed, however, when she
testified that she would not take him in.

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:44.380
The somewhat sympathetic judge sent Charlie
to Father Flanagan’s Boys Town.

00:03:44.380 --> 00:03:47.450
But the stay here was almost as short as his
last incarceration.

00:03:47.450 --> 00:03:51.610
After just four days, he ran off with another
young offender named Blackie Nelson.

00:03:51.610 --> 00:03:54.030
They stole a car which they subsequently crashed.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:58.240
Still, they made their way to the home of
Blackie’s uncle, a World War 2 veteran and

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:03.020
underworld figure who gave the young hoodlums
free board and food in exchange for the proceeds

00:04:03.020 --> 00:04:05.880
from armed robberies that he made them commit.

00:04:05.880 --> 00:04:08.380
During their third robbery the two boys were
caught.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:11.780
This time Charlie was sent to the Indiana
School for Boys in Plainfield.

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:14.209
Here he stayed for three years.

00:04:14.209 --> 00:04:18.459
Charlie would later claim that his small stature
led to him being constantly raped and sodomized

00:04:18.459 --> 00:04:21.499
by other inmates as well as by school employees.

00:04:21.499 --> 00:04:26.099
He also recalled that he was constantly picked
on by the guards, who would continually find

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:30.069
fault with him, beating him with leather straps
and wooden clubs.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:35.069
An Angry Young Man

00:04:35.069 --> 00:04:38.580
One night, after being gang raped by a group
of older boys, he beat one of his attackers

00:04:38.580 --> 00:04:43.430
to just short of the point of death with an
iron bar as the boy lay sleeping.

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:47.099
Charlie then placed the bar under the bed
of one of his other attackers, successfully

00:04:47.099 --> 00:04:48.940
implicating him in the attack.

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:53.560
Charlie was exhibiting a trait that would
characterize his personality as an adult;

00:04:53.560 --> 00:04:59.430
he would hold in his anger for a time, only
for it too explode in an orgy of violence.

00:04:59.430 --> 00:05:04.439
Over the three years that he spent at Plainfield,
Charlie escaped no less than eighteen times.

00:05:04.439 --> 00:05:06.300
He was returned every time.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:11.300
In March, 1951 his sentence was increased
and he was sent to a minimum-security institution.

00:05:11.300 --> 00:05:16.229
He was sent to the National Training School
for Boys in Washington, D.C.

00:05:16.229 --> 00:05:18.990
Things here were very different to what Charlie
had known at Plainfield.

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:25.259
The facility was well run, the boys were treated
well and a genuine focus was placed on rehabilitation.

00:05:25.259 --> 00:05:28.469
Charlie liked it here but he had no interest
in being rehabilitated.

00:05:28.469 --> 00:05:33.400
He’d do his time but then he’d get back
to the life of crime that he was the only

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:34.400
life he knew.

00:05:34.400 --> 00:05:37.469
At around the age of fifteen, Charlie was
give a psychiatric assessment.

00:05:37.469 --> 00:05:40.979
He was found to be aggressive, antisocial
and illiterate.

00:05:40.979 --> 00:05:46.270
A caseworker reported that the boy was severely
emotionally traumatized and in serious need

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:47.710
of psychiatric treatment.

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:51.650
It was also noted that he had a higher than
normal aptitude for music.

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:56.949
On October 24th, 1951, Charlie was transferred
to the Natural Bridge Honor Camp in Petersburg,

00:05:56.949 --> 00:05:57.949
Virginia.

00:05:57.949 --> 00:06:01.469
Three months later, just weeks before his
parole hearing, he sodomized another inmate

00:06:01.469 --> 00:06:03.550
while holding a razor blade to his neck.

00:06:03.550 --> 00:06:08.370
He was reclassified as extremely dangerous
and transferred to a tougher high security

00:06:08.370 --> 00:06:12.559
facility – the Federal Reformatory at Petersburg,
Virginia.

00:06:12.559 --> 00:06:17.749
After seven months at the Federal Reformatory,
Charlie had racked up eight major violations.

00:06:17.749 --> 00:06:23.290
He was classified as ‘defiantly homosexual,
dangerous and safe only under supervision,

00:06:23.290 --> 00:06:24.979
with assaultive tendencies.’

00:06:24.979 --> 00:06:28.720
Towards the end of 1952, he was sent to a
higher security facility.

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:32.810
There, to the surprise of everybody, he transformed
into a model prisoner.

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:37.110
He took lessons in reading and math and began
working in the vehicle maintenance department.

00:06:37.110 --> 00:06:42.759
On January 1st, 1954, he was given a Meritorious
Service Award for his scholastic achievements.

00:06:42.759 --> 00:06:47.279
His application to his studies and his apparent
change of attitude led to Charlie being paroled

00:06:47.279 --> 00:06:49.120
on May 8th, 1954.

00:06:49.120 --> 00:06:53.300
He was put in the care of his aunt and uncle
but, within a month, the now nineteen-year-old

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:58.360
was back living with his mother, herself recently
released from prison.

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:02.300
Career Felon

00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:06.639
Six months after his release, Charlie married
a waitress by the name of Rosalie Jean Willis.

00:07:06.639 --> 00:07:09.710
Shortly thereafter a son, Charles Manson,
Junior, was born.

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:13.389
Charlie worked at a serious low-income job,
augmenting his pay by stealing cars.

00:07:13.389 --> 00:07:17.039
He used one of those stolen cars to move his
wife and baby to Los Angeles.

00:07:17.039 --> 00:07:20.629
The car had been taken from Ohio and authorities
were able to track it down.

00:07:20.629 --> 00:07:25.259
Charlie was charged with a federal crime for
taking the car across state lines.

00:07:25.259 --> 00:07:28.770
He received five years’ probation but, when
he failed to show up to a subsequent hearing,

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:29.999
he was arrested.

00:07:29.999 --> 00:07:33.599
With his probation revoked, Charlie was sent
for three years to the prison on Terminal

00:07:33.599 --> 00:07:36.009
Island, in San Pedro, California.

00:07:36.009 --> 00:07:39.539
After being there a few months, he was informed
that his wife was living with another man.

00:07:39.539 --> 00:07:43.569
Two years later, she obtained a decree of
divorce.

00:07:43.569 --> 00:07:46.589
In September, 1958, Charlie was released on
five years parole.

00:07:46.589 --> 00:07:50.259
He now extended his criminal earning potential
by becoming a pimp.

00:07:50.259 --> 00:07:53.129
He had a sixteen-year-old girl working for
him.

00:07:53.129 --> 00:07:57.159
Over the next year, he roamed around California
and New Mexico, committing crimes and repeatedly

00:07:57.159 --> 00:07:58.660
coming before the law.

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:02.969
In June, 1960 he fled to Laredo, Texas with
a California warrant out for his arrest.

00:08:02.969 --> 00:08:07.319
When one of his girls was arrested there for
prostitution, he was picked up and returned

00:08:07.319 --> 00:08:12.529
to Los Angeles to face a 10-year sentence
for cashing a forged treasury check.

00:08:12.529 --> 00:08:17.219
At the age of 26, he was sent to the U.S.
Penitentiary at McNeil Island, Washington.

00:08:17.219 --> 00:08:22.449
While serving his sentence he learned to play
the guitar and became interested in Scientology.

00:08:22.449 --> 00:08:26.110
During his time at McNeil Island, he also
became obsessed with the Beatles.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:30.860
Charlie had an inflated appreciation of his
own musical talent, claiming that he would,

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:34.620
with the right backing and training, be even
bigger than the Beatles.

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:37.810
Charlie became friends with an inmate by the
name of Alvin Karpis.

00:08:37.810 --> 00:08:42.580
This former Public Enemy Number One was a
former member of the infamous Ma Barker gang.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:44.880
He taught Charlie how to play the steel guitar.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:46.940
This further fuelled his musical obsession.

00:08:46.940 --> 00:08:52.380
In 1966, Charlie’s prison record noted that
he spent most of his free time writing songs,

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:55.320
accumulating 80 or 90 of them in a year.

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:58.690
Karpis later commented on the Charlie that
he knew at that time.

00:08:58.690 --> 00:09:02.530
He recalled that Manson was a master manipulator
of other people.

00:09:02.530 --> 00:09:07.450
Prison authorities also noted that he had
a tremendous drive to call attention to himself.

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:11.940
In June, 1966, Charlie was sent once again
to Terminal Island – this time in preparation

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:12.940
for early release.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:18.570
When that release day arrived on March 21st,
1967, he had spent more than half of his 32

00:09:18.570 --> 00:09:19.680
years behind bars.

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:23.820
He requested that the authorities let him
stay in jail but he was told that he had to

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:25.760
leave.

00:09:25.760 --> 00:09:29.630
Charlie Unleashed

00:09:29.630 --> 00:09:33.780
And so it was that the five foot nothing drifter
with the penetrating stare and gift of the

00:09:33.780 --> 00:09:39.680
gab wandered into the Haight-Ashbury district
of San Francisco with $35 in his pocket and

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:44.280
no plans except for a desire to make it big
in the music business.

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:47.890
Charlie moved into an apartment in Berkeley
and made money by panhandling.

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:52.680
Before long he had gotten to know a 23-year-old
assistant librarian at UC Berkeley named Mary

00:09:52.680 --> 00:09:53.680
Brunner.

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:55.680
He quickly won her over and moved into her
apartment.

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:59.710
Brunner came under Charlie’s spell and he
convinced her to widen out the home.

00:09:59.710 --> 00:10:02.830
Within a few months, there were eighteen young
women living with them.

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:06.020
Charlie introduced Mary and the other girls
to drugs and before long Mary had quit her

00:10:06.020 --> 00:10:08.820
job and become a devoted follower of Manson.

00:10:08.820 --> 00:10:11.390
The ‘family’ was beginning to take shape.

00:10:11.390 --> 00:10:15.580
With his female entourage and his guitar,
Charlie merged perfectly into the hippie culture

00:10:15.580 --> 00:10:18.150
that was then in full bloom in San Francisco.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:23.740
He refined his role as spiritual master, guru
and prophet, using mind control techniques

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:26.640
to get his girls to do whatever he wanted.

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:29.740
Most of the girls that he gathered around
him came from troubled backgrounds and suffered

00:10:29.740 --> 00:10:34.240
from insecurities that left them directly
about open to Charlie’s manipulations.

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:38.430
As well as breaking down their inhibitions
with mind control techniques, he used LSD

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:41.940
and amphetamines to control his ever-expanding
harem.

00:10:41.940 --> 00:10:46.200
After about nine months living in and around
San Francisco, Charlie began to despair of

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:47.200
the place.

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:51.880
It had, he asserted become too overrun with
African Americans and crime was rampant.

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:56.320
Of course, the ‘Family’ were doing their
bit to add to those crime statistics.

00:10:56.320 --> 00:10:59.350
They stole credit cards and used counterfeit
money to get what they needed.

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:05.030
They also stole a big yellow bus and painted
it black.

00:11:05.030 --> 00:11:08.080
The Family

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:11.800
Charlie and his followers took to travelling
by bus down the California coastline as far

00:11:11.800 --> 00:11:15.490
as Mexico and Texas, partying and committing
more crimes.

00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:19.420
After eighteen months of extended travel,
they finally settled in Topanga Canyon near

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:21.730
Los Angeles in a two-storey house.

00:11:21.730 --> 00:11:25.500
It was here that Charlie began gathering some
male members to the Family.

00:11:25.500 --> 00:11:29.980
The first was a teenager named Bobby Beausoliel,
who turned up one night for a party and then

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:31.960
stayed on as Charlie’s right-hand man.

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:36.140
Bobby had been staying with his music teacher
Gary Hinman not far from the Manson home.

00:11:36.140 --> 00:11:41.890
Bobby recruited an 18-year-old named Leslie
Van Houtein to the family in June, 1968.

00:11:41.890 --> 00:11:45.340
Around that time, Charlie and some of the
girls travelled to Los Angeles where he met

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:48.250
up with a record executive at universal studios.

00:11:48.250 --> 00:11:50.950
Former jail friend Phil Kaufman had arranged
the meeting.

00:11:50.950 --> 00:11:55.280
This was Charlie’s entry into the rich jet
set crowd and he turned on all his charm to

00:11:55.280 --> 00:11:56.500
make a good impression.

00:11:56.500 --> 00:12:00.410
Soon the ‘Family’ were rubbing shoulders
with the rich and famous at posh parties in

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:01.750
the Hollywood Hills.

00:12:01.750 --> 00:12:06.560
In the late spring of 1968, Beach Boys drummer
Dennis Wilson was driving away from Malibu

00:12:06.560 --> 00:12:09.050
Beach when he happened to pick up two hitchhikers.

00:12:09.050 --> 00:12:12.220
The girls were part of the Manson family and,
they quickly agreed to go back to his Beverly

00:12:12.220 --> 00:12:13.220
Hills home with Wilson on Sunset Boulevard.

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:16.970
The three made love that afternoon and then
Wilson left for a recording session, promising

00:12:16.970 --> 00:12:19.720
to return later to take up where they left
off.

00:12:19.720 --> 00:12:22.930
When Wilson returned home in the early hours
of the following morning, he was surprised

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:25.340
to see that a full-scale party was underway.

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:29.360
He was greeted in the driveway by a short
man with a scraggly beard who approached him,

00:12:29.360 --> 00:12:32.040
dropped to his knees and began kissing his
feet.

00:12:32.040 --> 00:12:35.730
The girls who Dennis had met earlier came
running out declaring, ‘This is the guy

00:12:35.730 --> 00:12:38.880
we were telling you about . . . this is Charlie.’

00:12:38.880 --> 00:12:42.810
Inside his home, Wilson found twelve more
women, most of them topless, lying around

00:12:42.810 --> 00:12:44.110
smoking pot.

00:12:44.110 --> 00:12:47.160
Manson told him that the girls were all there
for Wilson’s pleasure.

00:12:47.160 --> 00:12:50.060
Wilson was impressed with the sway that Charlie
held over the women.

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:53.900
He welcomed the ‘Family’ with open arms
and his home become the regular venue for

00:12:53.900 --> 00:12:55.700
Charlie orchestrated orgies.

00:12:55.700 --> 00:12:59.880
Wilson called Manson the Wizard and began
inviting influential showbiz friends to come

00:12:59.880 --> 00:13:00.880
and meet him.

00:13:00.880 --> 00:13:04.650
Dennis also allowed Charlie to use anything
he wanted – his Ferrari or Rolls Royce and

00:13:04.650 --> 00:13:07.900
all the food drink and drugs he or his groupies
wanted.

00:13:07.900 --> 00:13:11.870
Eventually Wilson’s manager became fed up
with the influence and expense that Manson

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:16.060
was having on his client and Charlie and the
girls were ordered out of the mansion.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:19.920
Rumors were also spreading of the children
of the rich and famous being given drugs and

00:13:19.920 --> 00:13:22.040
having sex under Charlies direction.

00:13:22.040 --> 00:13:26.160
Suddenly, the door to the Hollywood elite
lifestyle was slammed shut.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:29.280
Charlie’s planned for music career was also
shut down.

00:13:29.280 --> 00:13:33.940
This caused that familiar build up of jealousy,
anger and rage that would inevitably find

00:13:33.940 --> 00:13:36.120
expression in violence.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:40.400
Manson managed to convince the owner of a
former Western movie set, the Spahn Ranch,

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:44.990
in Chatswood, not far from Topanga Canyon,
to allow the family to live on the abandoned

00:13:44.990 --> 00:13:45.990
property.

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:49.280
The family now moved to the ranch, getting
by stealing and scavenging.

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:53.150
Charlie took to quoting the Bible to Family
members as they gathered round a bonfire during

00:13:53.150 --> 00:13:54.150
the evenings.

00:13:54.150 --> 00:13:58.510
He also interpreted Beatles songs, explaining
that the lyrics were directed toward them.

00:13:58.510 --> 00:14:03.490
He was obsessed with one song ‘Helter Skelter’,
telling his followers that the song envisioned

00:14:03.490 --> 00:14:07.470
an apocalypse brought on by a race war of
blacks killing whites.

00:14:07.470 --> 00:14:12.900
The blacks would win, he said, but would then
turn to Manson to lead the new world.

00:14:12.900 --> 00:14:16.640
Helter Skelter

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:19.000
For Charlie, however, the revolution was taking
too long.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:21.650
He wanted it to happen immediately.

00:14:21.650 --> 00:14:26.110
He began preparing family members for a series
of actions that would precipitate the black

00:14:26.110 --> 00:14:27.110
uprising.

00:14:27.110 --> 00:14:30.690
The first step would be to release an album
of music that would contain subtle messages

00:14:30.690 --> 00:14:33.010
that would foment the black revolution.

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:37.750
On May 18th, 1969, Terry Melcher, a producer
who Charlie had met through Dennis Wilson

00:14:37.750 --> 00:14:41.310
arrived at Spahn Ranch to listen to Charlie
and the girls sing.

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:44.010
Melcher made promises but never followed through
on them.

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:50.010
On July 25th 1969, Charlie ordered Bobby Beausoliel
and two women to the home of Gary Hindman,

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:52.480
the music teacher who Bobby used to live with.

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:57.090
Manson had heard that Hindman had inherited
$20,000 and he wanted it.

00:14:57.090 --> 00:14:59.000
Hinman refused to hand over the money.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:01.130
Charlie was called and he soon arrived.

00:15:01.130 --> 00:15:04.120
After screaming at Hinman, Charlie pulled
out a sword and cut off his ear.

00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:08.410
He then left, giving instructions to get the
money or kill Hinman.

00:15:08.410 --> 00:15:11.180
After three days, Bobby stabbed his former
teacher to death.

00:15:11.180 --> 00:15:13.950
Before leaving he and the girls wrote the
words ‘Political Piggy’ on the wall along

00:15:13.950 --> 00:15:18.060
with a panther paw in red to lay the blame
on the Black Panther movement.

00:15:18.060 --> 00:15:23.000
Bobby Beusoliel was arrested for the murder
on August 6th, 1969 after being caught driving

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:24.680
around in Hinman’s car.

00:15:24.680 --> 00:15:28.430
Manson was now ready to get his revenge on
Terry Melcher, the record producer who had

00:15:28.430 --> 00:15:29.430
let him down.

00:15:29.430 --> 00:15:33.670
On the evening of August 8th, he directed
followers Tex Watson, Linda Kasabian, Susan

00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:37.870
Atkins and Patricia Krenwinkel to the house
where he believed Melcher was living with

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:43.070
instructions to ‘totally destroy everyone
in it, making it as gruesome as possible.’

00:15:43.070 --> 00:15:48.330
The house was located at 1050 Celio Drive
but Melcher didn’t live there anymore.

00:15:48.330 --> 00:15:54.279
It was now occupied by famous director Roman
Polanski and his beautiful 8-month pregnant

00:15:54.279 --> 00:15:56.000
wife, actress Sharon Tate.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:58.480
That night, Polanski was in Europe on a film
project.

00:15:58.480 --> 00:16:02.900
His wife was entertaining guests at the property
– hairdresser Jay Sebring, screenwriter

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:07.600
Voyteg Frykowski and coffee empire heiress
Abigail Folger.

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:11.279
Arriving at the property, around midnight,
Watson climbed a telephone pole near the gate

00:16:11.279 --> 00:16:12.710
and cut the phone line.

00:16:12.710 --> 00:16:16.400
The car was then back to the bottom of a hill
that led to the house and the murder team

00:16:16.400 --> 00:16:18.150
walked up to find the victims.

00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:22.860
Watson thought the gate might be electrified
so he and the girls climbed a brushy embankment

00:16:22.860 --> 00:16:23.890
to get onto the grounds.

00:16:23.890 --> 00:16:27.290
Just then, car headlights came on from farther
up the property.

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:30.820
Ordering the women to lie down in the bushes,
Watson approached the vehicle and levelled

00:16:30.820 --> 00:16:35.500
his 22-caliber rifle at the driver, 18-year-ol
Steven Parent.

00:16:35.500 --> 00:16:39.420
Watson first slashed hm with a knife and them
shot him four times in the chest.

00:16:39.420 --> 00:16:42.850
Watson then ordered Linda Kasabian to keep
watch down by the gate.

00:16:42.850 --> 00:16:45.050
He and the other two women then made their
way to the house.

00:16:45.050 --> 00:16:47.800
The occupants were quickly gathered together
in the lounge.

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:52.310
When asked by Frykowski who they were, Watson
replied, “I’m the devil and I’m here

00:16:52.310 --> 00:16:54.029
to do the devil’s work.’

00:16:54.029 --> 00:16:58.029
Watson then began to tie the heavily pregnant
Sharon Tate and Jay Sebring together by their

00:16:58.029 --> 00:17:01.360
necks with rope he’d brought and slung over
a beam.

00:17:01.360 --> 00:17:05.730
When Sebring protested over the rough handling
of Sharon, Watson shot him and then stabbed

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:07.070
him seven times.

00:17:07.070 --> 00:17:11.121
Meanwhile Frykowski began struggling with
Susan Atkins, who repeatedly stabbed him in

00:17:11.121 --> 00:17:12.750
the legs and torso.

00:17:12.750 --> 00:17:14.980
Still Frykowski managed to get to the front
door.

00:17:14.980 --> 00:17:19.040
Seeing this, Watson rushed after him, meeting
up with him on the porch and smashing in his

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:21.850
head with the gun butt before shooting him
twice.

00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:24.820
Abigail Folger had managed to escape out onto
the yard.

00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:29.370
She was chased by Patricia Krenwikel who tackled
her and then stabbed her to death.

00:17:29.370 --> 00:17:31.980
The only remaining victim was now Sharon Tate.

00:17:31.980 --> 00:17:35.900
As she lay on the lounge room floor with a
rope around her neck she begged to be able

00:17:35.900 --> 00:17:37.750
to live long enough to have her child.

00:17:37.750 --> 00:17:42.910
But her pleas were ignored and either Watson
or Atkins stabbed her repeatedly, including

00:17:42.910 --> 00:17:47.270
in the abdomen, until both she and her unborn
baby were dead.

00:17:47.270 --> 00:17:51.770
Remembering Manson’s instructions to leave
a sign on the walls, Atkins wrote the word

00:17:51.770 --> 00:17:53.730
“PIG” with Tate’s blood.

00:17:53.730 --> 00:17:55.990
The very next day, the Family struck again.

00:17:55.990 --> 00:17:59.460
This time the victims were Leno and Rosemary
LaBianca.

00:17:59.460 --> 00:18:02.860
Unhappy with the messiness of the previous
night’s killings, this time Charlie went

00:18:02.860 --> 00:18:05.360
with the group to show them how it was done.

00:18:05.360 --> 00:18:08.980
Different accounts have been giving about
the exact happenings that night but we do

00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:14.710
know that Manson was in the house and he orchestrated
the tying up of the couple, He then left with

00:18:14.710 --> 00:18:15.710
orders that the couple be killed.

00:18:15.710 --> 00:18:16.710
They were finished off by Watson with a chrome
plated bayonet.

00:18:16.710 --> 00:18:21.000
Before leaving the words “WAR”, “Rise”,
“Death To Pigs” and “Healter Skelter’

00:18:21.000 --> 00:18:27.880
were written with the blood of the victims
on the walls and refrigerator door.

00:18:27.880 --> 00:18:30.840
Caught

00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:32.809
The murders caused a huge panic through Hollywood.

00:18:32.809 --> 00:18:36.250
The pressure was now on to solve the heinous
crimes.

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:40.090
The police got nowhere until they finally
linked the Hinman murder to the Tate-LaBianca

00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:41.090
killings.

00:18:41.090 --> 00:18:45.390
They knew that Bobby Beusoliel had lived with
a group of hippies at Spahn Ranch so they

00:18:45.390 --> 00:18:47.050
decided to pay the ranch a visit.

00:18:47.050 --> 00:18:50.970
Bobby’s girlfriend had told police that
Charlie Manson, the hippie guru, had ordered

00:18:50.970 --> 00:18:52.090
the killing of Hinman.

00:18:52.090 --> 00:18:55.200
Still there was no evidence linking the group
to the later murders.

00:18:55.200 --> 00:18:59.050
Then, in October, twenty-four Manson family
members, including Charlie, were arrested

00:18:59.050 --> 00:19:01.510
on charges of arson and grand theft.

00:19:01.510 --> 00:19:06.540
Susan Atkins was also taken into custody and
it was she who first began to spill beans.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:11.430
She bragged to a cellmate about killing Sharon
Tate, giving a detailed account and implicating

00:19:11.430 --> 00:19:13.190
Charlie as the mastermind.

00:19:13.190 --> 00:19:16.740
About the same time, police interviewed a
member of the Straight Satans motorcycle gang

00:19:16.740 --> 00:19:18.170
who was a Manson acquaintance.

00:19:18.170 --> 00:19:22.740
He told them that Manson had recently been
bragging about ‘knocking off’ five people.

00:19:22.740 --> 00:19:26.530
The first piece of physical evidence was a
fingerprint of Patricia Rewinkle that was

00:19:26.530 --> 00:19:28.730
found on Sharon Tate’s bedroom door.

00:19:28.730 --> 00:19:32.520
When other pieces of physical evidence were
recovered, the police were ready to send the

00:19:32.520 --> 00:19:33.710
case to court.

00:19:33.710 --> 00:19:37.600
Manson and the four people who had committed
the Tate-La Bianca murders were found guilty

00:19:37.600 --> 00:19:39.300
and sentenced to death.

00:19:39.300 --> 00:19:42.250
These penalties, however, would never be imposed.

00:19:42.250 --> 00:19:47.040
In 1972 the California Supreme Court declared
the state’s death penalty law unconstitutional.

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:51.210
Manson’s’ death sentence was commuted
to life imprisonment.

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:56.820
Charles Manson died on November 19, 2017,
of cardiac arrest having spent nearly fifty

00:19:56.820 --> 00:20:02.960
years behind bars for his orchestrating of
the crimes that shook the world in 1969.

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:30.910
He was 83 years of age.

